# NG-RT-REFRACTION: ray-traced refraction of glass and shop windows, day half (designs
# S:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3H-DESIGN.md, S:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3G-DESIGN.md, S:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3E-DESIGN.md, F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3D-DESIGN.md,
# F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3C-DESIGN.md, F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3B-DESIGN.md and F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3-DESIGN.md,
# «## Приёмка»; physics F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION2-DESIGN.md). One editor session in F:/BistroFoliageProj,
# B16_Bistro_Street: frames of the shop window - path tracer | path tracer with the camera 50 cm aside |
# Translucency.Refraction ScreenSpace | HardwareTraced | HardwareTraced with Translucency.RefractionComposite 0 |
# HardwareTraced again | the same with Reflections.HitLighting 1 | the same with the camera 50 cm aside | the knockout
# frame with Reflections.Method ScreenSpace | HardwareTraced and path tracer with the window pair deleted | from inside
# the empty shell looking back at the window wall, path tracer | raster | raster Albedo - one camera (except the shift pair
# day_pt_shift / day_rt_shift and the experiments 3D D5, 3E D3), one exposure, one time, one tier.
# What is behind the glass (3H, S:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3H-DESIGN.md): there is NO interior in this content (0
# BistroInterior entities in the scene, 0 interior meshes in the project). Behind the shop window stands the empty
# shell of the building; the band x935-1080 y185-235 behind the upper right sash is the underside of the slab
# Paris_Building_01_paris_building_01_4279 (MASTER_Concrete_Smooth, n=(0,1,0)) of the empty shell. The statement is:
# raster and path tracer show the SAME surfaces behind the glass with the same brightness - never "an interior".
# The numbers before 3H (До, Hardware GI, run scn-1128-135823; the first run scn-1128-134820): the band L_lin day_rt
# 0.0123 / 0.0086 against day_pt 0.2447 / 0.2523; refr_split 0.0038 / 0.0023; the pane day_rt 0.1273 / 0.1265 against
# day_pt 0.1692 / 0.1704; the pass "Translucency: Ray Traced Refraction" 2.008 ms at 1787x657 with the path end from
# the cards (the day_rt dump, editor.log:16575), 0.180 ms muted (the day_rt_mute dump, :18061), 2.561 ms with the path
# end lit in place (the refr_split dump of line 131, :19475) = 4.52 ms at 1080p. The pass numbers are read from
# editor.log of the run folder: the reply files line_NNN_profile-dump.txt are empty ({"id":1,"ok":true}).
# The causes (3H D1-D3): (1) the window had three sheets - the duplicate _4713 of the inner sheet _4875 made the
# ray "leave" the glass twice and bend up (day_pt wall 0.1858, sash 0.0596 with it; 0.0907, 0.0346 without);
# (2) the shell seen from behind was one-sided, and the back face of a one-sided material is a black occluder for
# every hit (the GI-BACKFACE-HIT rule); (3) at Reflections.HitLighting 0 the path end read the surface cache cards,
# black there even for a two-sided material. 3H: _4713 deleted from the content, MASTER_Concrete_Smooth,
# MASTER_Concrete_Grooved, MASTER_Wood_Painted3 two-sided in the content, and the refraction path end is lit in place
# at every tier (the card branch deleted, one shader variant). The new reference day_pt (k1_pt, the knockout without
# _4713): the band 0.2634, the wall 0.0907, the sash 0.0346, the pane 0.1637.
# The radiance cache (3G D3): the refraction pass requests the cells its path ends read (the cache's request table,
# marked the next frame) - [day_probes] reads it in the radiance cache's log line.
# Open (3H D5, D4): the band lit in place 0.10 against 0.26 of the path tracer (-61 %) is the bounce of the hit
# (Common/GIHitLighting.glslh, the GI-TEMPORAL2 design's file), named, not held here; why the cards read black on
# the back of a two-sided material is not needed once the card branch is gone.
# The break (3G D5): scn-1128-122309 stopped at the step after day_mute_ss (frames 256 after Reflections.Method
# HardwareTraced came back under HardwareTraced refraction): "the editor closed the connection", run_capped exit=1
# peak 8986 MB; no day_rt_b, refr_split, day_rt_shift - the run noise on Hardware GI was never measured. The cause is
# not proven, so day_mute_ss is the last step with the glass: every frame a statement reads stands before it, and
# only the recorded experiments (the glass deleted) come after it.
# One branch (3H D3): the end of a refraction path is lit in place at every tier (GIHitRadianceLit +
# RadianceCacheRequestMark), whatever Reflections.HitLighting says - the row now selects the reflection hits only.
# day_rt is HitLighting 0 (High), refr_split HitLighting 1 (Cinematic) of one camera: the band and the pane of the
# two are equal within the noise 4.94 (the branch is one), and so are their pass times.
# The knockout of [day_rt] (3C D4). "day_rt differs from day_ss" is not a statement: the hit the camera sees reads
# the same scene copy, a thin sheet does not bend the ray, the tint is the same BaseColor. The trace is proven by
# switching its answer off in the same session instead: day_rt_mute is HardwareTraced with
# Translucency.RefractionComposite 0 (the glass cell ignores the trace), day_rt_b is day_rt again 512 frames later
# with the camera still (the run noise). Measure: mean |delta| of (R+G+B)/3 (0..255) over the pane mask = rectangle
# x540-1260 y170-630, pixels where day_pt > 8; |day_rt - day_rt_mute| >= 2 x |day_rt - day_rt_b| (Software GI noise
# 3.996 in scn-1128-113551; Hardware GI: the day_rt_b of this run).
# The path tracer is the reference: GlobalIllumination + Reflections PathTraced (the tracer pairs them). The raster
# frames keep Reflections / GI HardwareTraced; only Translucency.Refraction changes between day_ss and day_rt.
# The tier (D7): every group of the preset is pinned at High before any row (a group level drops that group's rows,
# so the pins come first); the benchmark preset (perf index 45 and 89 on one GPU within 8 minutes) chooses
# nothing in this run. An unattended run keeps every Quality change in this process (QualityState::KeepInSession):
# machine.json is never written; the tail still clears the rows. There is no group "Level" command: the next run
# starts from the machine's own selection.
# D1: Reflections.TranslucentFrontLayer 0 is set on purpose (the Low / Medium value; High alone would give 1).
# HardwareTraced refraction must draw the front layer it needs by itself - the day proves the consumer declares its
# dependency, it is never pinned to 1 here.
# The window rule (D6): a GPU time is a budget number only when the window is free - in BOTH dumps of a pair (ss
# and rt) "ClearMainFramebuffer" <= 0.2 ms, and their "GPU frame" differ by less than 2x; else the number is not
# a measurement and the run is repeated. Budget at 1080p = ms x 2073600 / (viewport width x height), the
# viewport size from editor.log (1787x657 today = 1.17 Mpx). Every measured capture has its own profile-dump
# (reply line_NNN_profile-dump.txt) right before it.
# The measures (S:/aftmp/3h/meas.py): L_lin = mean of the sRGB-decoded (R+G+B)/3 (0..1) over a rectangle of the
# 1787x657 frame - the band x935-1080 y185-235, the wall x940-1040 y260-300, the right sash x1105-1250 y185-455, the
# pane x540-1260 y170-630 (the pane mask: pixels where day_pt > 8) - an absolute measure, as the night (3D D3); "at
# least 4x darker" = a pane-mask pixel whose L_lin in the frame is <= 0.25 x its L_lin in day_pt. The noise 4.94 =
# the largest mean |delta| (8-bit levels) of a window frame between the two runs of До (frames_triage.py: day_rt
# 1.98, day_pt 3.48, day_rt_b 2.83, refr_split 2.88, day_rt_edge 4.94; S:/aftmp/3h/triage.out); the band's own noise
# in L_lin: day_pt ±0.004 (3 %), day_rt ±0.002; scripts/Dev/frames_compare.py.
# The shift pair (3G D4): the camera 50 cm aside (-346,300,-905, the same direction) moves the window ~150 px RIGHT
# (the left edge of the lower left sash x537 in day_rt -> x~687; the upper right sash x935-1250 -> x1085-1400 in
# day_rt_shift of scn-1128-113551). day_pt_shift is the path tracer at that camera, so day_rt_shift is held to the
# same rectangle x1085-1230 y185-235 of its own reference, never to day_pt of the other camera.
# The experiments (3D D5; 3E D3, D4), recorded, not judged unless the statement says so: day_mute_ss is
# day_rt_mute with Reflections.Method ScreenSpace: whether the grey gradient of the left column (light at the top,
# black at the bottom, where day_pt shows the sky and the brick wall; also in day_rt_mute, absent in day_rt_open)
# stays - the glass's own reflection layer, not the refraction trace (3E D4, 3G D9, open).
# day_rt_open / day_pt_open delete the window as the pair it is - _4711 (facing out) AND _4875 (facing in), two
# Entity "Delete" rows, the scene is never saved - and show the shell behind the window without the glass, raster |
# path tracer. One sheet alone is an invalid state (3H D7): the absorption is never taken off without the exit face,
# so the whole pane reads green (k2_pt / k2_rt). in_back_pt / in_back_rt / in_back_base look from inside the shell
# back at the window wall (the pair still deleted), path tracer | raster | raster Albedo: a wall the path tracer sees
# from inside and the raster does not is the raster culling the back faces of a one-sided material (3E D3, 3G D10);
# 3H makes MASTER_Concrete_Smooth, MASTER_Concrete_Grooved and MASTER_Wood_Painted3 two-sided, recorded.
# refr_split also proves Reflections.HitLighting 1 (the Cinematic value) builds - the reflection method does not refuse.
# Frame wait: `frames N` (N presented frames). Every capture stands >= 256 frames after the last
# GlobalIllumination.Method switch or camera position move (GI accumulation converged; else the opaque pixels
# drift); day_rt_edge alone is a turn taken after 32 frames, recorded, never compared with a still frame.
# The camera faces the cafe shop window Bistro_Research_Exterior_Paris_Building_01_paris_building_01_bottom_4711
# (MASTER_Glass_Exterior, StaticMeshGlass; pane pivot -108,197,-719, centre ~y 320) from 3 m out on the terrace;
# the window is the closed pair _4711 (outward) + _4875 (inward), the duplicate _4713 is gone from the content (3H D1).
# One exposure: AutoExposure off (at the scene's own ManualExposureEV100), back on in the tail. The night half is
# NG-RT-REFRACTION-NIGHT.scn: a `set` dirties the scene, and Open Scene would stop at its confirm popup.
Проект ../BistroFoliageProj/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/B16_Bistro_Street.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Textures High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Filtering High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Shadows High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Reflections High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: PostProcess High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Effects High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: AntiAliasing High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: ResolutionScale High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Shading High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: PathTracing High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Foliage High"
Дано run Anti-Aliasing "Anti-Aliasing: TAA"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Resolution.Percent 100"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Reflections.TranslucentFrontLayer 0"
# The profile-dumps carry GPU times only with GPU profiling on (Profiler "GPU"; off, every scope reads gpu 0.000).
Дано run Debug "GPU profiling: On"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position -370,300,-861
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.8806,0.07,0.4738
Дано set 6039035132485441499 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.AutoExposure false
